{
  "about": "Where Toolsmith looks (03 Part 2 q2: search sources are data, never code). A bundle may add rows. Each row names its reader; a row whose reader or host this code does not know is left out. Shelves and catalogs are read while a plan is made, only under the Bridge subject toolsmith:search (the search Yes names every host, wizard step 4). The fetch rows and the downloads are read by the Core itself, only while a build runs, after the plan Yes that names their hosts. Web rows need the owner's own key and are off otherwise. Dropped after checking 2026-10-30: Stack Overflow's API (its rules on keeping text for an AI could not be read and look like a no; Stack Exchange libraries come through Kiwix) and Openverse (its search answers nothing, an open outage).",
